        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Dennis Rodman\n- TV Shows: The Rodman World Tour\n- Books: Bad As I Wanna Be\n- Teams: Detroit Pistons, San Antonio Spurs, Chicago Bulls, Los Angeles Lakers, Dallas Mavericks\n- Organizations: MTV, NBA\n\nFacts:\n- Dennis Rodman was born on May 13, 1961.\n- Dennis Rodman is an American retired professional basketball player who played in the NBA for the Detroit Pistons, San Antonio Spurs, Chicago Bulls, Los Angeles Lakers, and Dallas Mavericks.\n- The Rodman World Tour was a television talk show hosted by Dennis Rodman.\n- The Rodman World Tour aired on MTV for its 1996 season.\n- Bad As I Wanna Be is Dennis Rodman's first autobiography.\n- Bad As I Wanna Be was published in 1996.\n- Dennis Rodman wrote Bad As I Wanna Be during the 1995-96 season while he was a member of the record-setting Chicago Bulls team.\n- The Chicago Bulls team Dennis Rodman played on in the 1995-96 season went on to win the NBA Championship.",
